EF AI Workspace (#153): artifacts that work like Claude's. Owner request 2026-10-23: "make the outputs (artifacts)
work like Claude's".

- Versions (hooks/Artifacts/useArtifacts.ts, ArtifactVersion.tsx): entries that share an identifier (else a type and
  title) are versions of one artifact, as in Claude. The menu shows «الإصدار i من n» for the open artifact only; it
  used to list every artifact of the chat by time. Auto-open and streaming are unchanged.
- Switcher (ArtifactSwitcher.tsx): «المخرجات في هذه المحادثة» lists each artifact of the chat once, by its newest
  version.
- Try fixing (ArtifactFixButton.tsx, SandboxArtifactTabs.tsx): when the Sandpack preview reports an error, one press
  sends the artifact's title and the error to the chat. Files, skills and quotes staged in the composer are not
  attached to it; hidden on shared links and while a reply is being written.
- Open in new tab (utils/artifactTab.ts, ArtifactOpenTab.tsx): an HTML page, SVG drawing or Markdown document in a tab
  of its own. The tab is a blob page with no script of its own; the artifact runs only inside a sandboxed srcdoc frame
  without allow-same-origin (an opaque origin, no top navigation), opened with noopener. Tailwind and the EF font are
  added as in the panel. Hidden on phones; React keeps the full screen.
- Code files (Artifact.tsx): the `language` attribute is kept, and Claude's `application/vnd.ant.code` opens in the
  code view instead of falling through to the HTML template.
- RTL: the panel's slide-in offsets and the version menu's position follow the reading direction.
- Tests: the panel tests follow per-artifact versions, and the download tests open the document menu of patch 0024.

